    "intro_html":  "Massaman is the gentlest of the Thai curries and the only one built for a tough cut of meat. It gets its character from dry warm spices, cloves, cinnamon, cumin, and nutmeg, rather than from raw chile heat, and the potatoes and peanuts turn it into a full dinner rather than a sauce. Each bowl comes in at {{cal}} calories and \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a serving\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
